rnment is  standing firm  that they will not hold back these laws  that the government that the farmers  are perhaps being misled now opposition  parties have chimed in  expressing support to a national strike  that was called by the farmers today  this has led the government to react and  call these protests political  the government points out that  opposition parties were in power in the  past or when contesting elections  have actually proposed laws very similar  to the ones that this government has  executed  they also allege that these parties are  now trying to pander to the ever  important voting bank of farmers  well the farmers have had delhi under  siege for almost two weeks and the  pictures we're seeing you can see a lot  of disruption now today's  strike how much support do the farmers  have amongst the general population  well farmers definitely do have support  rebecca when we look at this national  strike  transport unions have supported it there  is an expectation that fruit and  vegetable supplies will be hit  bank unions and other unions that also  express support  however farmers have said that this  protest will only be the strike will  only be  from 11 am to 3 pm local time because  they do not want to disrupt all those  goals  they do not want to inconvenience anyone  they say this is a symbolic protest  especially in the run-up to the sixth  round of talks they will have for the  government tomorrow  right namisha at jayaswal in delhi  thanks very much for the update  you
 

